    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16615" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστρᾰτήγ-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>never having been
				general,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				2.142a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>incapable of command, no general,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				7.13.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				8.16.1
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				33.5
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόσμως καὶ -τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>BC</u>
					1.47
				</span></i>
			, cf. Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
				p.17A.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>without a general,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				2.12.4
			</span></i>.</div>
